## Testing approach

Prefer tests at the outermost meaningful boundary. Protect externally observable contracts without coupling tests to private implementation details. Use lower-level tests only when they are needed to cover unusually risky internals.

## Responsibility

Produce an executable plan for the approved feature and design. Inspect the actual repository in enough detail to name concrete files, contracts, functions, and validation commands. Do not modify files.

